{"name":"Red Cent","hex":"#ad654c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red cent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A copper penny.","A very small amount of money."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_cent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Large cent","blocks":[{"text":"The United States large cent was a coin with a face value of 1⁄100 of a United States dollar. Its nominal diameter was 11⁄8 inch (28.57 mm). The first official mintage of the large cent was in 1793, and its production continued until 1857, when it was officially replaced by the modern-size one-cent coin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/1819_cent_obv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_cent"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/NNC-US-1793-1C-Flowing_Hair_Cent_%28chain%29.jpg/500px-NNC-US-1793-1C-Flowing_Hair_Cent_%28chain%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/NNC-US-1793-1C-Flowing_Hair_Cent_%28chain%29.jpg/1280px-NNC-US-1793-1C